      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Definition of Pronoun"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "A pronoun is a word used in place of a noun to prevent repetitive usage.",
        "Major categories include Personal, Possessive, Reflexive, Demonstrative, Interrogative, Relative, and Indefinite pronouns.",
        "Personal pronouns change forms based on person (1st, 2nd, 3rd), gender, and case (nominative, objective, possessive).",
        "Relative pronouns (who, whom, which, that) introduce relative clauses and connect them to antecedent nouns."
      ],
      "id": "detdjx9"
    },
